_model: proposition
---
title: Proposition 6
---
order: 6
---
short_label: XII.6
---
statement: Pyramids of the same height with polygonal bases are to one another as their bases.
---
proof:

Let there be pyramids of the same height with the polygonal bases *ABCDE* and *FGHKL* and vertices *M* and *N.*

I say that the base *ABCDE* is to the base *FGHKL* as the pyramid *ABCDEM* is to the pyramid *FGHKLN.*

Join *AC, AD, FH,* and *FK.*

<figure class="diagram">
<canvas id="canvas_0" width="400" height="280" tabindex="0"></canvas>
<noscript><img alt="XII.6 diagram" src="propXII6.gif"/></noscript>
